// Game: Postretro
// Format: Standard
// Reflection lake: manual test map for reflection-probe capture exclusion on a
// lake over 50 m across. See reflection-lake-test.README.md for the expected
// classification of every feature and what to look for.
// Axis-aligned box brushes; 1 map unit = 0.0254 m; map coordinates, Z up.
// Keep comments free of braces and quotes and
// never leave a blank line inside an entity block. A bare comment marker with
// no text after it also breaks the parser.
// Fluid water is declared in content/dev/start-script.ts; no data script.
// ----
// Compile: cargo run -p postretro-level-compiler -- content/dev/maps/reflection-lake-test.map -o content/dev/maps/reflection-lake-test.prl
// Run:     cargo run -p postretro-tool -- run --install-root . maps/reflection-lake-test.prl
// ----
// LAYOUT, one hall, interior x 0 to 3840, y 0 to 3840, 97.5 m square:
//   Shore     floor z 0, ceiling z 2112, 53.6 m. Walls yellow west, red east, green north, stone south.
//             The shore is 832 u, 21 m, wide from each wall to the water.
//   Lake      x 832 to 3008, y 832 to 3008, 2176 u = 55.27 m square, surface z -48, bed z -160.
//   Quay      the shore walls, 16 thick, bed to z 0, ring the lake.
//   Dock      north shore, x 1408 to 1536, y 2608 to 3008, deck z -40 to 0 on four legs.
//   Boathouse north shore, x 2368 to 2752, y 2816 to 3200, half over the water, roof z 192 to 216.
//   Posts     P1 to P5 and P7 in the water, 12 u square, bed to z 96. P6, purple, is the always override.
//   Rails     on the north quay: thin bars x 864 to 1376, a thick capped rail x 1792 to 2304.
//   Crates    north shore beside the dock, and one sunk into the dock deck.
//   Never     purple long wall on the north shore, x 768 to 1792, y 3232 to 3264.
//   Start     1920 664 on the south shore, in the dark, facing north across the lake.
//   Probe     an authored reflection_volume, the hall interior, binds the whole lake to one
//             probe. Derived, the lake splits into 8 probes, under the dock and around the
//             boathouse, each with a smaller W. Delete the box to see that split.
//   Lights    eleven lamps and the boathouse light, each its own pool with dark hall between.
//             Every falloff range is under half the distance to the nearest other light, so
//             no two pools overlap. Lamps hang at z 160 to 224; the roof stays dark. Only the
//             centre lamp, the north shore lamp and the boathouse light are runtime lights.
//             A blue spot at z 752 points straight down over the centre lamp, range 5000,
//             cone 10 to 80, and is the one light whose reach is not a pool.
// ----
// AT W 55.2 m the size threshold t is about 17.2 m, 677 u, and the thin floor f
// about 0.41 m, 16 u. Each brush comment below names its expected class.
{
"classname" "worldspawn"
"wad" ""
"_tb_mod" "dev"
"_tb_def" "external:../../../sdk/TrenchBroom/postretro.fgd"
"_lightmap_density" "0.125"
